---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Oliver, 58, Saarland. Four-year build toward the Transcontinental Race 2030."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="about">
				<p class="eyebrow eyebrow--center about__label">About</p>
				<h1 class="about__title">Fifty-eight years old.<br />Four years across Europe.</h1>
				<hr class="rule about__rule" />

				<p>I'm Oliver. 58 years old, based in Saarland, Germany.</p>

				<p>
					In May 2026 I started a four-year build toward the Transcontinental Race 2030. This site
					documents that build: training, kit, rides, doubts, data, the lot. Honestly.
				</p>

				<p>
					The race is a ~4000 km self-supported ride across Europe, ridden in roughly two weeks. The
					route changes each year. The qualification standard is high enough that most applicants
					don't get in.
				</p>

				<p>Four years should be enough. We'll see.</p>

				<p>
					The handle "onepedalstroke" is the practice the whole project reduces to. Long rides are
					not made of grand efforts. They are made of single, repeated pedal strokes, sustained
					over time. So is anything else worth doing.
				</p>

				<p class="about__email">hello @ onepedalstroke . cc</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
